  @doc """
  The temporal-adjacency reading of tracing spans, and deliberately nothing
  more than today's discovery applied to spans: one `LogTrace` per `trace_id`
  (`case_id` = `trace_id`) whose `activity_sequence` is the spans'
  `service_name` values ordered by `{start_time, span_id}` (lexicographic
  ISO8601, ties broken by `span_id`). `parent_span_id` is NEVER read here --
  this is what a miner that only sees timestamps and a correlation id would
  conclude. Traces are sorted by `trace_id`.
