  @typedoc """
  The two evidence classes over one span set, plus both of their differences.

    * `observed` - `evidence: :parent_child_link`, one edge per distinct
      (parent `service_name`, child `service_name`) pair, `frequency` = the
      number of parent/child links with that pair.
    * `adjacent` - `evidence: :temporal_adjacency`, `traces_from_spans/1` ->
      `dfg_from_traces/1` re-tagged; `frequency` = the number of consecutive
      `start_time` pairs, summed over traces. Same span set, so the two
      frequency scales are comparable per pair.
    * `inferred_only` - adjacent edges whose pair no parent/child link
      supports: what adjacency invented.
    * `observed_not_adjacent` - observed edges whose pair adjacency never
      produced: real causality adjacency cannot see.
    * `orphans` - `{span_id, parent_span_id}` for every span whose parent is
      absent from the input (sampled out, uninstrumented). Never an edge,
      never dropped silently; the span itself stays in the adjacency arm so
      the caller can tell "no evidence" from "adjacency invented it".

